Z||000000||Jules||04-05-2001||08:40 PM||||OK, you asked...I showed codes 13,23,24,32,35, & 44. In the Haynes manual, it shows the parts related to the codes and I have replaced EVERYTHING it indicated (oxy, MAT, & TPS sensors and EGR & IAC valves--I think these were stressed from a vacuum leak). I've also replaced the alternator, so I know it's good. For whatever reason, that damn light STILL COMES ON!! (oh the insanity!!) All my fluids are full & still pumping properly, fan still working, no leaks anywhere... BUT, when that light is on, I'm noticing decreased fuel economy and a hesitation when I hit the gas. For that, I've dumped some $30-a-can fuel injector cleaner in it, no help. It has new plugs & wires too so I don't think that's it.<P>As you can see, I've tried just about everything. If anyone has any more ideas, I'll listen...as long as they don't include something like "just put black tape over the light" ...I get ideas like that from the bastards that want to charge $50/hour who are supposed to be able to actually FIX IT, the right way.||||reg||1
