Z||000007||Formula88||04-06-2001||08:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Turbo1dr:<BR><B> Thanks for calling Auto Technicians like myself "Bastards".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">   I'd really like to help you get your car fixed but I don't seem to be as knowledgeable as you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Now, now.  Play nice.  I've dealt with my share of "Bastards" when trying to get my car fixed.  I've also dealt with some awesome, knowledgeable technicians.  Don't take it personally just because Jules has dealt with idiots in the past.  From my personal experience, I can say all the techs at Crown Pontiac in Raleigh NC are as dumb as a toenail.  And their service manager, Mat Mann, has all the customer service skills of a sweat gland.  Now, Leith Pontiac, out in Wendell NC, they have great service, knowledgeable techs, and on time delivery at the state cost, fixed right the first time.  I would imagine my experieces are fairly typical.  The quality of the tech is going to vary greatly from dealer to dealer, or garage to garage.  Even ASE doesn't mean what it used to.  I've dealt with backyard shadetree mechanics who were more knowledgeable than the 22 year old ASE tech as some dealers.  Again, this is just my experience.  Good auto techs are a valuable commodity.  When you find a good one, stick with them!<P>Now, Jules.  I have to agree with some other posts.  Clear your ECM and then try again.  Check the codes and start from scratch.  You may have fixed a bunch of stuff and something else is still wrong, or something new could have happened in all the part swapping.  Go back to square one.  Do not pass go, do not collect $200.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>||||reg||7
Z||000008||Turbo1dr||04-06-2001||11:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B> Now, now.  Play nice.  I've dealt with my share of "Bastards" when trying to get my car fixed.  I've also dealt with some awesome, knowledgeable technicians.  Don't take it personally just because Jules has dealt with idiots in the past.  From my personal experience, I can say all the techs at Crown Pontiac in Raleigh NC are as dumb as a toenail.  And their service manager, Mat Mann, has all the customer service skills of a sweat gland.  Now, Leith Pontiac, out in Wendell NC, they have great service, knowledgeable techs, and on time delivery at the state cost, fixed right the first time.  I would imagine my experieces are fairly typical.  The quality of the tech is going to vary greatly from dealer to dealer, or garage to garage.  Even ASE doesn't mean what it used to.  I've dealt with backyard shadetree mechanics who were more knowledgeable than the 22 year old ASE tech as some dealers.  Again, this is just my experience.  Good auto techs are a valuable commodity.  When you find a good one, stick with them!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree on what you say. That is true. I don't go around calling all of my customers "bastards" because one of them griped about his/her bill. I don't think Jules or anyone else for that matter, would have liked it if I would've replied to his post with a statement like this:<BR>"You stupid fool! You've spent ALL THAT money for nothing and still have the same problem. I can't believe you think you can actually FIX your car the FIRST TIME."  <P>I think that would offend a lot more people on this board than just him.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>86 SE Fiero converted to GT (Buick Turbo V6 transplant in progress)<P><B>78 Malibu</B> 3.8L Turbo Buick<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/turbowonder/Malibu/Homex.html" TARGET=_blank>TURBO WONDER</A><BR>Best 8th: 1.548, 6.62@106.32  3450lb<BR>TE-70 3 bolt, Ported Stock Iron Heads and Intake<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/turbowonder/Malibu/Modifications_files/Intercooler.jpg" TARGET=_blank>2.5 stock intercoolers</A><BR>Vernon Swindell, Jr.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DRH||04-06-2001||02:11 PM||||Turbo1dr,<BR>I didn't read it that Jules was calling all techs bastards... Just the ones that told him to "fix" it by putting tape over the light. That would seem to be a justified use of the term.<P><BR>Jules,<BR>As mentioned above, you need to clear the codes if you haven't already. There should be a small single wire connector near the battery on most models you can disconnect for a few seconds. OR you can just disconnect the battery for a few seconds. <P>Next confirm you have no codes. Drive the car until the light comes on and check codes again. Hopefully it will just be one or two now. Haynes manual should have procedure for checking codes. <P>PS: Most of those codes could have been caused by the vacuum leak, I assume it's been fixed...<P>David.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jules||04-07-2001||05:03 PM||||MY GOD!! some of you are more sensitive than WOMEN!!! <BR>For the record, yes, I meant that the $50/hr techs that suggested black tape are the bastards in question...there are some idiots in Illinois who obviously think they deserve that kinda money for sh*tty advice like that. And, no, I did not think I could fix this car right the first time. It has been a constant work in progress for over 6 months now and $200 doesn't scratch it. More like 1300, so don't think I'm just b*tchin for fun. <BR>Also for those of you who haven't read anything else I've written, I'm a woman, not some beer-swilling garage gnome. I mentioned my troubles with the car and some people were concerned enough to ask for the codes I was reading. That's all this was about. Not insulting anyone or getting anyone's feathers nasty. Now, forget it. I'll fix my "friggin" car myself.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Will||04-07-2001||07:23 PM||||Spirited, isn't she?<P>Jules, just ignore the ones who bi-- are sensitive and pay attention to the ones who give you advice. I believe there were several who suggested you clear the old codes before going any further. Have you done that yet?<BR>Did you ever find the vacuum leak?<p>[This message has been edited by Will (edited 04-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jules||04-08-2001||04:56 PM||||I cleared the codes...had to diconnect the battery to get some of the parts on. Didn't want the one person willing to help me get jolted. (haha) To be truthful, I haven't re-checked them to see what it's reading now. The fact I've spent so much money & not solved the problem is so distressing I can't stand it. When I sent it off to have the vacuum leak fixed, the bare spot in my front lawn for the 4 days it was gone made me a basket case. I literally sobbed like a child every time I looked out the window. Now that it's above freezing outside (as I have no garage to swill beer in) I'll check into this on my next day off work & let the ones who care know some more info. <BR>Thanks!! ||||reg||1
Z||000013||gabriel||04-09-2001||03:36 PM||||&gt;MY GOD!! some of you are more sensitive than WOMEN!!! <P>  Now Jules,  men aren't sensitive, they are *touchy*.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  However, I've got to agree with you on that issue .....<P>&gt;More like 1300, so don't think I'm just b*tchin for fun. <BR> <BR>  Wow!!  I'd be fuming!!!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>&gt;I'll fix my "friggin" car myself.<P> I agree with that.  Then no one can let you down but yourself. <P>Let us know how you fare with this.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Jules||04-10-2001||05:17 AM||||Well, so much for that idea. Today I was on my way to a safe place to check those codes and the old hag died on me. I swear every time I try to better that car, something craps out on me. BTW, I think it's the fuel pump.<BR>Let ya know when it returns to the land of the living.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Jules||04-14-2001||04:00 PM||||Well, Good Friday being good after all, the Fiero runs again!! It was the fuel pump, so now I'm on the road with a smile once more. I thought since it was running again, I'd get to those codes, and what I'm getting now is a 32. Guess it's better to show just 1 than the 6 I got before. I've replaced the EGR valve already. Would it be the solenoid causing the light to still come on? ..anyone?||||reg||1
